  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Figshare dataset for the <em>Pirum gemmata</em> genome shows an early but real reuse signal: it has been cited once in the scholarly literature and is documented as reused in two downstream records. The record is open access and remains lightly used overall, so the impact story is still emerging rather than broad.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2017 and deposited in Figshare by Multicellgenome Lab, this dataset provides genome assembly and annotation files for <em>Pirum gemmata</em>, alongside predicted coding sequences and peptides. Its strongest evidence of impact is scholarly reuse: OpenAlex records one citation, and the reuse graph identifies two downstream references, including an article in <em>eLife</em> that cites the dataset as a source.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing literature points to continued relevance within molecular evolution and protist genomics. The single citing article is in <em>eLife</em> and sits in a biology/evolutionary context, which fits the dataset\u2019s genome-focused scope. That one citation is an early signal rather than a mature citation profile, but it does show the dataset is being used in later research rather than remaining purely archival.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Stewardship signals support accessibility and reuse. The dataset is openly available in Figshare, with OpenAIRE matching multiple open instances of the resource, including versioned records. That versioned availability can make reuse easier by giving later authors a stable, citable source for the genome materials they need.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Other attention channels are quiet in the available record: there are no recorded online mentions in Event Data and no scite citation breakdown. DataCite also shows no logged views or downloads in the supplied digest, and teaching adoption is only represented by a WorldCat holdings search link rather than a confirmed course listing. Overall, the record suggests a specialized research asset with demonstrated but still limited downstream uptake.</p>",
